# Home APM sidecar environment (BYOH mode).
# Copy to deploy/homeapm.env and fill in your Home Assistant long-lived token.
#
# In DEMO mode you do NOT create this by hand — deploy/seed-token.sh generates
# deploy/homeapm.env from .ha-runtime/token.txt.
#
# FRESH CLONE: neither .ha-runtime/ nor ha-config/.storage/ is committed, so the
# seeded house has NO user account and NO token yet. Cast the stack first, open
# http://localhost:8123, finish the HA onboarding wizard, then mint a token at
# Profile (your name, bottom left) > Security > Long-lived access tokens >
# Create token. Full steps: deploy/NOTES.md > "First-run bootstrap".
#
# Only HA_TOKEN belongs here; HA_URL and OTLP_ENDPOINT are set on the service in
# casting.yaml / docker-compose.fallback.yml. GEMINI_API_KEY is optional and, if
# present, improves the console's ask-your-house answers.
HA_TOKEN=paste-your-home-assistant-long-lived-access-token-here
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
